{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1501995-control-freak-vampires","id":1501995,"title":"Control-Freak Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-02T19:33:29-08:00","id":1501995,"title":"Control-Freak Vampires","content":"Has anyone played or experienced, vampires, that are absolute control-freaks? Does anyone have examples in play? How did they manifest their controlling desires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T13:11:24-08:00","id":1502039,"title":"","content":"There was an example presented by one of Matthew Dawkins' videos that stuck with me, although it was for Masquerade. It was for a Malkavian Prince whose madness was paranoia. He was intelligent, polite and surprisingly sane, at least at first glance.<br /> <br /> His method of control was based on inflicting paranoia on others. A rumor here, suspicious evidence there, he would divide and conquer. When the big players were in conflict with each other, he would always be there, their gracious and trustworthy Prince, the one who does what is needed to keep things civil, their safe harbor in the storm. Should anyone try to usurp him, they would be struck down by everyone else, his role far too convenient to be removed. Thus he secured his power, connections and knowledge of his domain's secrets.<br /> <br /> <i>Duobus certantibus tertius gaudet </i> - &quot;While two argue, the third rejoices&quot;\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-03-2023, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T01:51:30-08:00","id":1502292,"title":"","content":"Ain't all Vampires control freaks ?<br /> <br /> They can deny it all they want, but all of them need a hard to come by ressource (Vitae) compared to the Kine who can buy it in any store in Western Countries at least.<br /> <br /> I'd definitively remind all players that with their powers came great weaknesses and that the older a vamp, the greater is tendency to want to control everything and everyone around her !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T21:42:10-08:00","id":1502343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1501995-control-freak-vampires?p=1502292#post1502292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ain't all Vampires control freaks ?<br /> <br /> They can deny it all they want, but all of them need a hard to come by ressource (Vitae) compared to the Kine who can buy it in any store in Western Countries at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, that resource is one of many things that can set off a distinct loss of control that can have worse/longer-lasting consequences the more powerful and/or less-humanlike you are, and becoming less humanlike is a consequence of, among other things, encountering reminders that you are no longer a living person.<br /> <br /> I've <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1329402-embrace-as-punishment?p=1330637#post1330637\">previously</a> described Requiem as a game where the title characters have a brutal resource-management puzzle they have to spend their nights with and institutional corruption is a particularly effective tool for lightening the load on that account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T22:17:17-08:00","id":1502346,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Vampires need to control as much of themselves and the world around, otherwise they get devoured by the Beast inside, which makes for very compelling charatcers IMHO. How long can one neonate hold to his pre-Embrace morality before it becomes a dangerous liability, not just for himself but the peoples he cares about ? And how long can an ancient Elder can deny she's still just human, beneath all those centuries of horrors, and how does it affect her - and those around her ?<br /> <br /> Edit <br /> <br /> Also to bounce off your old post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I can't help but wonder if peoples see Vampiric Condition as largely positive because of the easy access to our basic needs (at least in the West). Scarcity is largely a thing of the past (and perhaps our future) and it makes it hard to conceive the existential horror of having to struggle for food and drink.<br /> <br /> And Vampires are in a state worse than us for their preys have the means to eradicate them if they ever realize the Kindred exist. Control, at all level, from personal to institutional have to be enforced strictly for survival. It must be quite taxing and create a negative feedback by increasing the chances of Frenzy because of the mental pressure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 02-07-2023, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T18:07:08-08:00","id":1548506,"title":"","content":"After reading a bit from a newer version of the Vampire's Player's Guide(late-90's), that stated: Vampires manipulate, not control directly; this got me thinking that, a control-freak vampire won't last very long, in a sense. Sure, he could have a politics of five and be very astute, but, over time, he'll make a mistake that will cost him or her their unlife. It's better to manipulate than directly control, i.e, be the Primogen and advise the prince, rather than be a target for angry neonates. All it really takes is a good placed stake, and the dawn. <br /> <br /> Now, as an ST, I would create a control-freak Prince, as part of the story, and make that NPC as interesting as possible, i.e., out-witting the PCs, every chance they got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}